# Phase 2 — Bring GCC 14 Online

---

## 1. Wire Backend Into GCC

Take:

```text
toolchain/gcc14/backend/gcc/config/oasis16/
```

and patch GCC 14 source tree.

Update:

```text
config.gcc
config.sub
```

Add target triplet:

```text
oasis16-unknown-elf
```

---

## 2. Build Minimal Compiler

Configure:

```bash
--enable-languages=c
--without-headers
--disable-shared
--disable-threads
--disable-libssp
--disable-libstdcxx
--disable-nls
```

Only build:

```text
C compiler
```

No:

```text
C++
Ada
Fortran
OpenMP
```

---

## 3. Restrict Initial Backend Scope

Native mode:

```text
HImode
```

Register width:

```text
16-bit
```

No support for:

```text
32-bit arithmetic
division
floating point
long long
```

yet.

---

## 4. Make GCC and GAS Agree

Ensure:

```text
operand printers
constraint definitions
register names
immediate formats
```

exactly match GAS syntax.

Acceptance:

```bash
oasis16-elf-gcc -S add.c
```

assembles successfully.

