# Prototype Success Definition

The prototype is considered successful when the following works on macOS:

```bash
toolchain/scripts/build-darwin-gcc14.sh \
    --prefix "$PWD/.toolchain/oasis16" \
    --gcc-src /path/to/gcc-14 \
    --binutils-src /path/to/binutils \
    --jobs 8
```

and then:

```bash
.toolchain/oasis16/bin/oasis16-elf-gcc \
    -ffreestanding \
    -nostdlib \
    toolchain/runtime/crt0.o \
    examples/c/hello_int.c \
    -T toolchain/runtime/oasis16.ld \
    -o hello_int.elf
```

followed by:

```bash
oasis16-elf-objdump -d hello_int.elf
```

and:

```bash
oasis-elf2img hello_int.elf hello.img
```

producing a runnable OASIS binary image.

